const e="karnatak-university-inter-zonal-youth-festival",u=2022,t="Read all 14 pages of the UNIFEST 2022-23 notice. It is a past-edition notice (Vth Zone PG Zone Youth Festival, 27-28 December 2022), so every date, fee and contact is a starting suggestion kept as a Variable. The notice prints the bank account number of the President, P.G. Gymkhana, and two more personal e-mail addresses of the President; these are not copied. The notice prints no marks, prizes, points or grades, and no judging criteria with numbers. Differences inside the notice: Debate and Elocution language (item rule says Hindi or English, Eligibility Rules A.10 says Kannada and English or Hindi, Director's letter says Kannada, English or Hindi for Zonal and Inter-Zonal); Folk Orchestra size (item rule up to 12, Annexure 9 plus 3); Poster Making time (item rule 2 hours 20 minutes, Annexure 150 minutes); Mehandi time (item rule 2 hours, Annexure 150); theatre language (Eligibility Rules A.12 Kannada or English, One Act Play item rule Hindi, English or any regional language); item times differ between the Annexure table (min and max) and item rules. The Director's letter has no reference number or date printed.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Karnatak University UNIFEST: the Zonal and Inter Zonal Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival. Read these rules before you register.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Send your application, signed by the Chairman of the Department or the competent authority, to the President of the P.G. Gymkhana on or before {{EntryDeadline}}. The entry fee is {{EntryFee}} The festival is at {{Venue}}.",Notes:["A team that is the only entry for an item gets no prize.","Bring the eligibility certificate in duplicate (in the proforma) and your identity card.","The events may be rescheduled if something sudden happens."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"About the Festival",Items:["UNIFEST is the Karnatak University Youth Festival. It has a Zonal (Intercollegiate) stage and an Inter Zonal stage.","The festival has 5 families of events: Music, Dance, Literary Events, Theatre and Fine Arts. The items, their times and the number of participants and accompanists are in the Annexure table.","The events may be rescheduled because of any sudden development. The Chief or Co-ordinator (Events) may reschedule an event and announce the programme in advance.","Teams compete in the order decided by a draw of lots held by the organisers.","At the Zonal and Inter Zonal level, the Debate is held in Kannada, English or Hindi. At the Inter-University level, the Debate is held only in English or Hindi.","Host colleges send the list of the First and Second place winners of each event to the President of the P.G. Gymkhana, with a copy to the Director, within two days after the event."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Only a bonafide, full-time student can take part. The student must be enrolled for a degree, a postgraduate degree or a diploma course.","The course must last at least one academic year. Its examination must be conducted by the University after the 12th class examination under the 10+2 pattern (from a recognised Board of Higher Secondary or Senior Secondary in the country) or an equivalent examination.","Only degree students (not PUC) who are less than 25 years of age on 1st July of the academic year in which the activity is held can take part.","Bring the eligibility certificate in duplicate, in the proforma, and your identity card.","A copy of the S.S.L.C. Marks Card must be attached.","The entry form and the eligibility form can be photocopied if needed.","The Student Welfare Officer or Cultural Co-ordinator of the college certifies on the eligibility form that the student is a degree student of the college and is within the age limit. The Principal also signs it, and it carries the college seal.","Only one entry per event per college is allowed.","A college can send at most 40 participants, including accompanists.","A college can enter any or all of the events.","Colleges are asked to organise their team so that, as far as possible, a minimum number of participants take part in the maximum number of events. This is because the number of participants is restricted at the South Zone Youth Festival."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Send your application, signed by the Chairman of the Department or the competent authority, with all the details, to the President of the P.G. Gymkhana, Karnatak University, Dharwad, on or before {{EntryDeadline}}. Contact: {{SubmitTo}}.","The Principals of the colleges send the entry fees with the necessary details of the participants to the concerned host colleges.","Fill in the eligibility form for each participant and accompanist: college name, father's name (in block letters), name of the participant (in block letters), date of birth, item of participation and previous participation (in detail). The participant signs it, and a passport-size photograph is affixed.","Fill in the entry list (Annexure-IV) for each item: name of the college, item family (Music, Dance, Theatre, Literary or Fine Arts), name and date of birth of each participant, whether student or professional, name and type of the sub-item, number of times the participant took part in the National Youth Festival, and remarks. Use a separate form for each item. The Cultural Co-ordinator signs it with name and date.","Folk/Tribal Dance, Classical Dance and Skit teams give 3 copies of a brief note with the entry form at registration. For Folk/Tribal Dance the note gives the theme and the text of the song if any. For Classical Dance the note describes the dance story, if any, and the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English. For Skit the note is a synopsis of the theme with the language of presentation.","A play in a regional language needs its synopsis, with a translation in English or Hindi, given to the in-charge of the competition on the day of registration.","Teams must report to the organisers in time. The contingent leaders make sure that the team reports for each event at the time and in the order announced by the organisers."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["The entry fee is {{EntryFee}}","Pay by demand draft or challan in favour of the President, P.G. Gymkhana. Direct payment into the bank account of the President, P.G. Gymkhana, is also allowed, with the counter receipt produced."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["Vth Zone (PG Zone) Youth Festival, 2022-23 edition: {{ZonalFestivalDates}}.","Inauguration: {{InaugurationTime}}.","Inter Zonal UNIFEST, 2022-23 edition: {{InterZonalDates}}.","South-East Zone UNIFEST, 2022-23 edition: {{SouthEastZoneDates}}.","Last date to submit applications: {{EntryDeadline}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["Zonal festival: {{Venue}}.","Inter Zonal UNIFEST: {{InterZonalVenue}}.","South-East Zone UNIFEST: {{SouthEastZoneVenue}}."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Levels",Items:["The 2022-23 notice lists three stages: the Zonal UNIFEST, the Inter Zonal UNIFEST and the South-East Zone UNIFEST. It also mentions the Inter-University level and the National Festival.","The Zonal festival is held in five zones. Host colleges report the First and Second place winners of each event to the President of the P.G. Gymkhana within two days after the event.","Some items have longer time limits at the national level. For Classical Vocal Solo and Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion and Non-Percussion) the minimum and maximum time are 12 and 15 minutes. For Elocution at the national festival the minimum and maximum time are 7 and 10 minutes.","Debate and Elocution speakers can speak for at most 5 minutes in the Zonal festival and 10 minutes in the National Festival."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries and Team Size",Items:["Only one entry per event per college is allowed. For Folk Orchestra, each institution can send only one team.","A college can send at most 40 participants, including accompanists.","The Annexure table gives participants, accompanists and the total (P+A) for each item: Classical Vocal Solo, Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion), Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion) 1+2=3; Light Vocal (Indian) 1+2=3; Western Vocal (Solo) 1+2=3; Group Song (Indian) and (Western) 6+3=9; Folk Orchestra 9+3=12; Western Instrumental Solo 1+2=3; Folk/Tribal Dance 10+5=15; Classical Dance 1+3=4; Quiz 3; Elocution 1; Debate 2; One Act Play 9+3=12; Skit 6+3=9; Mime 6+2=8; Mimicry 1; each Fine Arts item 1 and Installation 4."]},{Key:"payments",Title:"Travel and Stay",Items:["The participants and the team managers are not paid TA/DA or transport.","Accommodation in the open hall of the hostels is provided, if possible."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["Teams must bring their own musical instruments and other special items needed for their items.","The accompanists, if needed, are arranged by the participating teams, up to the limits shown for each item.","Only suitable Indian and Western musical instruments can be used for the Indian and Western Group Song items.","For Classical and Folk Dance, tape recorders are not allowed.","Participants bring their own fine-arts material, musical instruments and make-up material.","In debate, elocution and any speech, no remarks against religion, caste, creed, person or party are allowed."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging and Time Limits",Items:["The decision of the panel of judges is final and binding on all.","No prize is given if there is only one entry for an item.","For Light Vocal (Indian), Western Vocal (Solo), Elocution and Mimicry (the items marked with *), the grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds. For all other items the grace time is 30 seconds.","The qualities judged for each item are listed under each competition. The notice prints no marks."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Other Notes",Items:["The notice also prints the inauguration on the first day of the Zonal festival, and the Inter-University and National Festival time limits for some items."]}],Documents:[{Title:"UNIFEST 2022-23 notice, rules and Annexure (PDF)",Url:"https://www.kud.ac.in/admin_panel/noti/Conduct%20of%20Vth%20Zone%20(PG%20Zone)%20Youth%20Festival%20on%2027th%20and%2028th%20December%202022%20at%20K.U.%20Campus,%20Dharwad.pdf"}]},i=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23) (participants 1) and UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["An individual item is for one participant, with up to the number of accompanists shown for that item."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- An individual item is for one participant, with up to the number of accompanists shown for that item.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23) and UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["For a team item, the number of participants and the number of accompanists are counted separately; the Annexure table gives both and their total (P+A)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- For a team item, the number of participants and the number of accompanists are counted separately; the Annexure table gives both and their total (P+A).`}],a=[],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Classical Vocal Solo (Hindustani or Karnatak)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music a); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).","Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.","Sufficient thought and care must be exercised in the choice of raga and composition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Movie songs."],"Judging":["Qualities judged: swara, tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.\\n- Sufficient thought and care must be exercised in the choice of raga and composition.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Movie songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: swara, tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music b); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).","Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Qualities judged: taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music c); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).","Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":["Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian raga system."],"NotAllowed":["Casio (electronic keyboard) instruments.","Western music."],"Judging":["Qualities judged: swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Item can be presented in either Hindustani or Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration of performance: 10 minutes at most (8 minutes at least).\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum number of accompanists: two per team.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Instruments of western origin adapted to the Indian raga system.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Casio (electronic keyboard) instruments.\\n- Western music.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- At the national (Inter-University) level the minimum and maximum time is 12 and 15 minutes."},{"Title":"Light Vocal (Indian)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music d); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of the song: between 4 and 6 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: 2 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The number of accompanists is not more than two."],"Allowed":["Only non-film songs, geet, ghazal, bhajan, shabad and abhangas."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Qualities judged: swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration of the song: between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: 2 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The number of accompanists is not more than two.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only non-film songs, geet, ghazal, bhajan, shabad and abhangas.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music e); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of the song: between 4 and 6 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: 2 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The number of accompanists is not more than two.","The language of the song is English only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Cinema songs."],"Judging":["Qualities judged: composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration of the song: between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: 2 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The number of accompanists is not more than two.\\n- The language of the song is English only.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Cinema songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."},{"Title":"Group Song (Indian)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music f); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["A team presents two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.","The songs are Indian songs, which can be in a regional language."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time for the group song: 10 minutes (8 minutes at least), not including setting time.","Setting time for a group: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum 6 singers in a group. Three accompanists can play instruments.","Only suitable Indian musical instruments can be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Movie songs."],"Judging":["Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A team presents two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.\\n- The songs are Indian songs, which can be in a regional language.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum time for the group song: 10 minutes (8 minutes at least), not including setting time.\\n- Setting time for a group: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum 6 singers in a group. Three accompanists can play instruments.\\n- Only suitable Indian musical instruments can be used.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Movie songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Group Song (Western)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music g); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The group songs are in the English language."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time for the group song: 10 minutes (8 minutes at least), not including setting time.","Setting time for a group: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum 6 singers in a group. Three accompanists can play instruments.","Only suitable Western musical instruments can be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The group songs are in the English language.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum time for the group song: 10 minutes (8 minutes at least), not including setting time.\\n- Setting time for a group: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum 6 singers in a group. Three accompanists can play instruments.\\n- Only suitable Western musical instruments can be used.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music h); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The team may present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes (the Annexure table prints 8 and 10).","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Each institution can send only one team.","The team has up to 12 participants (the Annexure table prints 9 participants plus 3 accompanists, 12 in all).","The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix of both.","Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They wear different dress from the student participants so that they can be easily identified.","The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The team may present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes (the Annexure table prints 8 and 10).\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institution can send only one team.\\n- The team has up to 12 participants (the Annexure table prints 9 participants plus 3 accompanists, 12 in all).\\n- The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix of both.\\n- Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They wear different dress from the student participants so that they can be easily identified.\\n- The professional accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team."},{"Title":"Western Instrumental Solo","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Music i); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The participant plays western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.","The participant performs any one genre or style, or fuses various genres or styles of western music."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: at least 6 minutes and at most 8 minutes.","The time is counted from immediately after the final announcement by the organisers.","Setting time: 3 minutes for each participant.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Maximum 2 accompanists are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The participant plays western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.\\n- The participant performs any one genre or style, or fuses various genres or styles of western music.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: at least 6 minutes and at most 8 minutes.\\n- The time is counted from immediately after the final announcement by the organisers.\\n- Setting time: 3 minutes for each participant.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Maximum 2 accompanists are allowed."},{"Title":"Folk/Tribal Dance","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Dance a); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The dance can be either primitive or a folk dance (Indian style), but not a classical one."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of the dance: not more than 10 minutes (8 minutes at least in the Annexure table).","Time for setting sets or instruments: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","At most 10 participants are allowed per team. The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix of both.","Five accompanists are allowed.","Give 3 copies of a brief note with the theme and the text of the song, if any, with the entry form at registration.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Tape recorders."],"Judging":["Qualities judged: rhythm, formation, expression, costume, make-up, sets and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The dance can be either primitive or a folk dance (Indian style), but not a classical one.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration of the dance: not more than 10 minutes (8 minutes at least in the Annexure table).\\n- Time for setting sets or instruments: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- At most 10 participants are allowed per team. The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix of both.\\n- Five accompanists are allowed.\\n- Give 3 copies of a brief note with the theme and the text of the song, if any, with the entry form at registration.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Tape recorders.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: rhythm, formation, expression, costume, make-up, sets and overall effect."},{"Title":"Classical Dance (Indian)","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Dance b); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The classical dance can be from any of the approved schools of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam and Odissi."],"TimeAndFormat":["The participant is allowed up to 15 minutes, including time for preparation (12 minutes at least in the Annexure table).","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","Maximum three accompanists are allowed.","Give 3 copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English, at registration."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Tape recorders."],"Judging":["Qualities judged: taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, footwork and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The classical dance can be from any of the approved schools of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam and Odissi.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The participant is allowed up to 15 minutes, including time for preparation (12 minutes at least in the Annexure table).\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- Maximum three accompanists are allowed.\\n- Give 3 copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English, at registration.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Tape recorders.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: taal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, footwork and general impression."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Literary Events a); Eligibility Rules A.11; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Each institute sends a team of three persons.","There is a written preliminary round, and teams are selected for the final. The final is oral, with audio-visual questions."],"TimeAndFormat":["The written test is in English. It has 50 objective-type questions and lasts 30 minutes.","The rules for evaluation, the time to reply to a question and the type of round are given before the competition starts."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Group or team discussion during the competition."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Each institute sends a team of three persons.\\n- There is a written preliminary round, and teams are selected for the final. The final is oral, with audio-visual questions.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The written test is in English. It has 50 objective-type questions and lasts 30 minutes.\\n- The rules for evaluation, the time to reply to a question and the type of round are given before the competition starts.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Group or team discussion during the competition."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Literary Events b); Eligibility Rules A.10; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Each institute is represented by one speaker.","The item is prose or poetry, not a song."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each speaker can speak for at most 5 minutes in the Zonal Festival (10 minutes in the National Festival).","Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds.","Medium of expression: Hindi or English (Eligibility Rules A.10 says Kannada and English or Hindi).","The performance is judged in one language."],"Rules":["The subject or topic is announced in the managers meeting (Eligibility Rules A.10: at least 24 hours earlier).","The order of the speakers is decided by a draw of lots."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Remarks against religion, caste, creed, person or party."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["At the national level the minimum and maximum time is 7 and 10 minutes."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Each institute is represented by one speaker.\\n- The item is prose or poetry, not a song.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each speaker can speak for at most 5 minutes in the Zonal Festival (10 minutes in the National Festival).\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds.\\n- Medium of expression: Hindi or English (Eligibility Rules A.10 says Kannada and English or Hindi).\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The subject or topic is announced in the managers meeting (Eligibility Rules A.10: at least 24 hours earlier).\\n- The order of the speakers is decided by a draw of lots.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Remarks against religion, caste, creed, person or party.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- At the national level the minimum and maximum time is 7 and 10 minutes."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Literary Events c); Eligibility Rules A.10; Director Student Welfare letter","Sections":{"About":["Each institute is represented by two debaters. One speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST it.","The topic is announced 24 hours in advance."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each debater can speak for at most 5 minutes in the Zonal Festival (10 minutes in the National Festival).","Medium of expression: Hindi or English in the item rule. Eligibility Rules A.10 says Kannada and English or Hindi, with two participants (one for and one against) for each of Kannada and English (or Hindi) from each college. The Director's letter says the Zonal and Inter-Zonal Debate is held in Kannada, English or Hindi and the Inter-University Debate only in English or Hindi."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from paper.","Remarks against religion, caste, creed, person or party."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Each institute is represented by two debaters. One speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST it.\\n- The topic is announced 24 hours in advance.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each debater can speak for at most 5 minutes in the Zonal Festival (10 minutes in the National Festival).\\n- Medium of expression: Hindi or English in the item rule. Eligibility Rules A.10 says Kannada and English or Hindi, with two participants (one for and one against) for each of Kannada and English (or Hindi) from each college. The Director's letter says the Zonal and Inter-Zonal Debate is held in Kannada, English or Hindi and the Inter-University Debate only in English or Hindi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from paper.\\n- Remarks against religion, caste, creed, person or party."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Theatre a); Eligibility Rules A.12; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Judging is most likely on the qualities of the play, such as theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression."],"TimeAndFormat":["The play does not exceed 30 minutes (25 minutes at least in the Annexure table).","Time is counted as soon as the signal is given or the team starts giving an introduction, whichever is earlier. Empty stage to empty stage is followed strictly.","Up to 10 minutes are given for setting and removing the set and properties after taking charge of the stage.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The number of participants does not exceed nine. The number of accompanists does not exceed three.","The team brings its own set, stage property and make-up material. Light and general property, such as ordinary furniture, can be provided on advance information.","Languages: Hindi, English or any regional language of India. If the language is a regional one, give the in-charge of the competition a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi on the day of registration. Eligibility Rules A.12 says the play is in Kannada or English, and a play in another regional language needs an English translation submitted two hours before the start.","The team reports to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation.","The decision of the panel of judges is final and binding on all."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Accompanists on the stage. They speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Judging is most likely on the qualities of the play, such as theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The play does not exceed 30 minutes (25 minutes at least in the Annexure table).\\n- Time is counted as soon as the signal is given or the team starts giving an introduction, whichever is earlier. Empty stage to empty stage is followed strictly.\\n- Up to 10 minutes are given for setting and removing the set and properties after taking charge of the stage.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The number of participants does not exceed nine. The number of accompanists does not exceed three.\\n- The team brings its own set, stage property and make-up material. Light and general property, such as ordinary furniture, can be provided on advance information.\\n- Languages: Hindi, English or any regional language of India. If the language is a regional one, give the in-charge of the competition a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi on the day of registration. Eligibility Rules A.12 says the play is in Kannada or English, and a play in another regional language needs an English translation submitted two hours before the start.\\n- The team reports to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation.\\n- The decision of the panel of judges is final and binding on all.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Accompanists on the stage. They speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Theatre b); Eligibility Rules A.12 and A.13; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The item is judged on the qualities of theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time for each team: 10 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","At most six participants and at most three accompanists.","Give 3 copies of the synopsis of the theme, with the language of presentation, on the day of registration.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity and bitter insinuations."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music."],"NotAllowed":["Character assassination."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The item is judged on the qualities of theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum time for each team: 10 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- At most six participants and at most three accompanists.\\n- Give 3 copies of the synopsis of the theme, with the language of presentation, on the day of registration.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity and bitter insinuations.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Character assassination."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Theatre c); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Duration of the performance: 5 minutes at most.","Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","At most six participants per team (the Annexure table adds 2 accompanists)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Qualities judged: idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Duration of the performance: 5 minutes at most.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 30 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- At most six participants per team (the Annexure table adds 2 accompanists).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Theatre d); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each student artist gets at most 5 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institute is allowed."],"Allowed":["Mimicking the sound of machines and the speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Qualities judged: imitating skill, variety of voices and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each student artist gets at most 5 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit: 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institute is allowed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Mimicking the sound of machines and the speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Qualities judged: imitating skill, variety of voices and presentation."},{"Title":"On The Spot Painting","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts a); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The item is conducted on the spot. The participant paints on the subject given by the in-charge of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by a single participant.","The size of the painting is half imperial size, 22 inches x 15 inches. The host institute provides only the paper or sheet."],"Allowed":["Oil, water, poster or pastel colours."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The participant brings their own material, such as brushes and paints."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The item is conducted on the spot. The participant paints on the subject given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by a single participant.\\n- The size of the painting is half imperial size, 22 inches x 15 inches. The host institute provides only the paper or sheet.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Oil, water, poster or pastel colours.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The participant brings their own material, such as brushes and paints."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts b); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The item is conducted on the spot on the given topic or subject. The sheet size is 15 inches x 22 inches."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by one participant.","The collage has to be made from old magazines.","The organisers provide the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The participant brings their own scissors, paste and other things needed."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The item is conducted on the spot on the given topic or subject. The sheet size is 15 inches x 22 inches.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by one participant.\\n- The collage has to be made from old magazines.\\n- The organisers provide the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The participant brings their own scissors, paste and other things needed."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts c); Eligibility Rules A.14; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The item is conducted on the spot. The participant makes a poster on the subject or topic given by the in-charge of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 20 minutes in the item rule (150 minutes in the Annexure table)."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by one participant.","The organisers provide only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inches x 15 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The participant brings their own material."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The item is conducted on the spot. The participant makes a poster on the subject or topic given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 20 minutes in the item rule (150 minutes in the Annexure table).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by one participant.\\n- The organisers provide only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inches x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The participant brings their own material."},{"Title":"Clay Modelling","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts d); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The item is conducted on the spot. The topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by a single participant.","The host institute provides the clay."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The item is conducted on the spot. The topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by a single participant.\\n- The host institute provides the clay."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts e); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The subject is given on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by one participant.","The host university provides only the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The participant brings their own material."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The subject is given on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by one participant.\\n- The host university provides only the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The participant brings their own material."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts f); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["This art is known by different names in different regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli.","The medium and form of expression can be freehand, pictorial or descriptive."],"TimeAndFormat":["Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by one participant.","The participant makes the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers.","Only one medium is used: poster colours, flower petals, saw-dust, pulses or rice, without pasting."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The participant brings their own material."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This art is known by different names in different regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli.\\n- The medium and form of expression can be freehand, pictorial or descriptive.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Duration: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by one participant.\\n- The participant makes the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers.\\n- Only one medium is used: poster colours, flower petals, saw-dust, pulses or rice, without pasting.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The participant brings their own material."},{"Title":"Spot Photography","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts g); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.","Additional instructions are announced on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time limit: 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["A college or institution can send one participant.","The participant brings their own digital camera. The camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest begins.","The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they want."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.","Software such as Photoshop to enhance the images."],"Judging":["Digital images are judged on: impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The participant takes 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.\\n- Additional instructions are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time limit: 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A college or institution can send one participant.\\n- The participant brings their own digital camera. The camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest begins.\\n- The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they want.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.\\n- Software such as Photoshop to enhance the images.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Digital images are judged on: impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Installation","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts H); Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation.","This is a group activity. Four participants can take part, but they create only one installation."],"TimeAndFormat":["The Annexure table gives 150 minutes as the maximum time. The item rule prints no time."],"Rules":["The size of the installation must not be bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet.","Participants can use all the material used in other art items, such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling.","Participants can use waste material that is available in the surroundings, or bring any material from outside.","Participants compose or create their own images from the raw material."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Any already composed images or forms available in the market."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation.\\n- This is a group activity. Four participants can take part, but they create only one installation.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The Annexure table gives 150 minutes as the maximum time. The item rule prints no time.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The size of the installation must not be bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet.\\n- Participants can use all the material used in other art items, such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling.\\n- Participants can use waste material that is available in the surroundings, or bring any material from outside.\\n- Participants compose or create their own images from the raw material.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any already composed images or forms available in the market."},{"Title":"Mehandi","Source":"UNIFEST 2022-23 item rules Fine Arts 1) Mehendi; Annexure table (UNIFEST 2022-23)","Sections":{"About":["Due credit is given to originality, creativity and decorative art with aesthetic sense.","The mehendi must reach the palm-side forearm, with a minimum length of six inches."],"TimeAndFormat":["The total duration for completing the painting does not exceed 2 hours (the Annexure table gives 150 minutes)."],"Rules":["The participant brings their own mehendi and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Hand prints, any kind of mould and any kind of decorative materials."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Due credit is given to originality, creativity and decorative art with aesthetic sense.\\n- The mehendi must reach the palm-side forearm, with a minimum length of six inches.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The total duration for completing the painting does not exceed 2 hours (the Annexure table gives 150 minutes).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participant brings their own mehendi and other materials.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Hand prints, any kind of mould and any kind of decorative materials."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"ZonalFestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Vth Zone (PG Zone) Youth Festival, 2022-23 edition",Value:"2022-12-27 to 2022-12-28",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) (27th and 28th December 2022)"},{Key:"InterZonalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Inter Zonal UNIFEST, 2022-23 edition",Value:"2023-01-12 to 2023-01-13",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) important dates table (12th and 13th January 2023)"},{Key:"SouthEastZoneDates",Kind:"date",Label:"South-East Zone UNIFEST, 2022-23 edition",Value:"2023-01-27 to 2023-01-31",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) important dates table (printed: 27th to 31th January 2023)"},{Key:"EntryDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to submit applications",Value:"2022-12-17",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) (on or before 17-12-2022)"},{Key:"InaugurationTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Inauguration",Value:"10 am on 27th December 2022, Senate Hall, K.U. Dharwad",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Zonal festival venue",Value:{Name:"Karnatak University campus",Address:"Pavate Nagar",City:"Dharwad",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) (Karnatak University campus, Pavate Nagar, Dharwad)"},{Key:"InterZonalVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Inter Zonal UNIFEST venue",Value:{Name:"K.U. Dharwad",Address:"",City:"Dharwad",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) important dates table"},{Key:"SouthEastZoneVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"South-East Zone UNIFEST venue",Value:{Name:"Gulbarga University",Address:"",City:"Kalaburagi",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) important dates table"},{Key:"EntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee",Value:"INR 125 per person per event. An institution that competes in more than 10 events pays INR 1250 in total.",Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022); Eligibility Rules A.15"},{Key:"SubmitTo",Kind:"contact",Label:"Send the application to the President, P.G. Gymkhana",Value:{Name:"Prof. S. C. Shiralashetti",Role:"President, P.G. Gymkhana, Karnatak University, Dharwad (Department of Mathematics, Pavate Nagar, Dharwad 580003)",Phone:"9986323159, 8073501595",WhatsApp:"",Email:"scshiralashetti@kud.ac.in"},Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) signature block"},{Key:"UniversityOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Karnatak University office phone",Value:{Name:"Karnatak University, Dharwad",Role:"Post Graduate Gymkhana letterhead",Phone:"0836-2215371",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) letterhead (Phone: 0836-2215371)"},{Key:"DirectorStudentWelfare",Kind:"contact",Label:"Director, Students Welfare Section",Value:{Name:"Dr. S. K. Pawar",Role:"Director, Students Welfare, Karnatak University, Dharwad",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"Director Student Welfare letter; the notice prints no phone or email for him"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Notice printed in the circular",Value:[{Date:"2022-12-08",Title:"Vth Zone (PG Zone) Youth Festival, 27th and 28th December 2022",Text:"The P.G. Gymkhana, K.U. Dharwad organises the Vth Zone (PG Zone) Youth Festival on 27th and 28th December 2022 at the Karnatak University campus, Pavate Nagar, Dharwad. The two days of events begin with the inauguration at 10 am on 27th December 2022 in the Senate Hall.",Url:""}],Source:"P.G. Gymkhana covering letter (08-12-2022) (Ref. No: PG/GYM/2022-23/22)"}],l=[{Claim:"Eligibility, fees, dates, item rules, forms and the Annexure table of the Karnatak University UNIFEST 2022-23 notice.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own circular",Source:"Karnatak University, Dharwad - UNIFEST 2022-23 Rules and Regulations for the Intercollegiate (Zonal) and Inter Zonal Youth Festival (Student Welfare Section / PG Gymkhana notice)",Url:"https://www.kud.ac.in/admin_panel/noti/Conduct%20of%20Vth%20Zone%20(PG%20Zone)%20Youth%20Festival%20on%2027th%20and%2028th%20December%202022%20at%20K.U.%20Campus,%20Dharwad.pdf"}],m={TemplateKey:e,Year:2022,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,u as Year,m as default};
